    <p class="eyebrow">About the project</p>
    <h1>A smaller footprint for one-off email.</h1>
    <p class="page-lede">TempMail is a simple interface for a temporary inbox. It is designed to help people separate low-stakes sign-ups from an everyday email address.</p>
    <h2>How it works</h2>
    <p>When you open the mailbox, TempMail calls the Guerrilla Mail JSON API from a Cloudflare Pages Function. Guerrilla Mail creates and manages the address and its messages. This site does not operate its own mail server.</p>
    <h2>What it is—and is not</h2>
    <p>A disposable email address can reduce unwanted follow-up to a personal inbox. It is not an anonymity service, a secure mailbox, or a substitute for an address you need to retain. Messages are held by the provider, and other users may be able to access an address after it becomes available again.</p>
    <h2>Design principles</h2>
    <ul><li>Explain the service and its limits plainly.</li><li>Keep the interface lightweight and usable on small screens.</li><li>Do not add tracking scripts or retain message contents in this application.</li><li>Use the provider's documented operations rather than pretending unsupported actions work.</li></ul>
    <p>Learn more about <a href="/privacy/">privacy and data handling</a> or see the <a href="/faq/">frequently asked questions</a>.</p>
  </article>
</BaseLayout>
